Subject: [PATCH 400/443] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on 0399: release
 the prime's silent clip and wait out a reply that starts during the settle

The prime's silent clip was never released before the first mic start because releaseForMic returned 0 until something had been released, and the prime's own late release set no settle time. releaseForMic now releases any held clip when no real reply is speaking, the prime releases through the shared helper, and a clip still playing at mic start gets the full settle. A reply that starts during the 150 ms settle now makes the mic start wait until it ends, then release and settle again. The release log line prints only when a release ran. Tests assert the load() count when the mic callback runs through the real releaser, the prime cases, the speak-during-settle case, the settle remainder and a desktop Safari case.
